From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: bornaradusin <bornaradusin@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 121/121] PC5: a steering wheel on the console is the game's Logitech
 G29

A G29 (as PS4 and PS5 racing games take it) is found once the controller
is open: the user's controller when libScePad says its device class is a
wheel's, else the special port's first controller. The title logs what
the console answers (PW_WHEEL lines), reads it each frame, sets
PW_WHEEL=1 and publishes it to its sink (pw_wine_set_wheel). Wine patch
0957 makes the game a G29 Driving Force (046d:c24f) as a PC finds one by
USB, which DirectInput reads as a driving device: steering, accelerator,
brake and clutch, a hat and 24 buttons. In xinput mode the wheel is also
on controller 0: steering the left stick, the pedals the triggers. No
force feedback yet.
