+From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
+From: bornaradusin <bornaradusin@users.noreply.github.com>
+Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0000
+Subject: [PATCH] xinput1_3: A PS5 title's steering wheel as a Logitech G29.
+
+A PS5 title that finds a steering wheel on the console (a G29, which PS4
+and PS5 racing games take) sets PW_WHEEL=1 and keeps the wheel's state in
+its sink (pw_wine_wheel). xinput1_3 then makes the game a G29 Driving
+Force as a PC finds one plugged in by USB, 046d:c24f, the way dualsense.c
+makes the DualSense: a device in the server answered on a thread of the
+game's process as hidclass.sys answers a HID collection, with the
+registry keys plug and play leaves. Its input report is the Unix
+library's (pw_wheel.h, staged beside it): steering, accelerator, brake
+and clutch, a hat and 24 buttons, which DirectInput reads as a driving
+device. ntdll loads xinput1_3 at the start for it, as for the DualSense.
+There is no force feedback yet: the device takes no output or feature
+reports.
+
+diff --git a/dlls/ntdll/loader.c b/dlls/ntdll/loader.c
